# Built right

Modern stack. Strict layering. Test-friendly. Cloud-native.

---

# The architecture earns trust

Unite is built on patterns that scale: layered architecture, CQRS, transactional safety, no hidden coupling.

- **.NET 10 + Blazor Server** — Microsoft's strategic stack; no legacy framework debt
- **CQRS without MediatR** — explicit, debuggable handlers; reads and writes optimized independently
- **EF Core + Unit of Work** — every multi-step write is transactional; rollbacks are real
- **Telerik Blazor** — enterprise-grade UI components, licensed and supported
- **Azure-native** — App Service, Functions, Service Bus, Key Vault, Application Insights, Blob

*Net: the codebase passes the architect sniff test on day one.*

---

<!-- _class: section -->
<!-- _color: #F1554B -->

# Integration footprint

The reason ERPs fail isn't features. It's plumbing. Unite ships with plumbing.

---

# Wired into the systems brokers run

Out of the box, Unite speaks the protocols the back office already uses.

- **OneDigital Accounting Hub (AH)** — handoff/polling pairs for cash, accruals, journals, products, split intake
- **FinOps / Dynamics 365** — vendors, employees, transactions, fiscal periods, financial dimensions
- **Workday** — payroll both directions, time entries, project staffing, invoices
- **Mulesoft** — products and customers ingest with durable orchestration
- **Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD)** — internal *and* external user provisioning
- **Google Gemini + OCR** — AI-driven statement template authoring and column extraction

*Net: this isn't a standalone app — it's a hub.*

---

<!-- _class: section -->
<!-- _color: #F2B949 -->

# AI where it earns its keep

Not chatbot-bolt-on. AI inside the workflow.

---

# Mapping Studio — AI that actually saves time

Brokerages receive statements from hundreds of carriers, every one in a different format. Unite's Mapping Studio uses Google Gemini to turn that chaos into a structured pipeline.

- **Provider auto-detection** — point at a statement, get the carrier identified
- **Column mapping suggestion** — Gemini proposes mappings; humans approve
- **Value mapping suggestion** — carrier code → canonical GL/dimension
- **NL prompt → extraction script** — write rules in English, get executable code
- **OCR for PDFs** — region-select on the document, extract embedded text

*Net: onboarding a new carrier statement format drops from days to minutes.*

